#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SE2265 expect=noViolation domain=DD
#note "Latest disposition for subject 001 starts 2020-01-20. Row 1 is collected exactly on that date (boundary: equal is allowed), row 2 the day after (post-mortem), row 3 has an empty DDDTC (guarded out by non_empty) -> no violation."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset DD label="Death Diagnosis"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DDSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DDTESTCD type=Char label="Death Diagnosis Short Name"
col DDORRES  type=Char label="Result or Finding in Original Units"
col DDDTC    type=Char label="Date/Time of Collection"
---
S1 | DD | 001 | 1 | DTHCAUS | HEPATIC NECROSIS | 2020-01-20
S1 | DD | 001 | 2 | DTHCAUS | HEPATIC NECROSIS | 2020-01-21
S1 | DD | 001 | 3 | DTHCAUS | HEPATIC NECROSIS |
---

dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSTERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Disposition Event"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
col DSSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Disposition Event"
---
S1 | DS | 001 | 1 | MOVED TO RECOVERY | RECOVERY | 2020-01-10
S1 | DS | 001 | 2 | FOUND DEAD        | DEAD     | 2020-01-20
